<section class="wrap pad-bottom page-narrow-left prose">
    <h2 class="h2">What we store</h2>
    <p>Your name, email address, town and a securely hashed password (we never store your password itself). We also store your listings, messages, ratings, reports and support requests so the marketplace can work.</p>

    <h2 class="h2">Email authentication</h2>
    <p>Email is the primary authentication and verification method for accounts. Existing phone details are not used to sign in.</p>


    <h2 class="h2">Browsing</h2>
    <p>Guests can browse without an account. To suggest listings, we keep which listings you opened during your visit, linked to a random session key, and to your account if you are signed in.</p>

    <h2 class="h2">Reports and evidence</h2>
    <p>Evidence attached to a report is visible only to the admin team and is kept private.</p>

    <h2 class="h2" id="seller-data">Seller identity verification</h2>
    <p>To apply to sell, you provide your legal name, sex, date of birth, residential address and images of both sides of a valid government ID. The ID images are stored in private server storage and can be viewed only by authorized marketplace admins for application review. They are deleted 30 days after the admin decision. If the application has not been decided, the files remain restricted to admins until the decision.</p>
    <p>Seller identity checks use Didit’s hosted verification service for government-ID checks, face liveness and face matching. When you choose to continue, your identity details and biometric face data are processed by Didit under its own privacy and retention terms. Review the provider’s privacy notice in the hosted verification flow before giving separate biometric consent. The marketplace stores Didit’s session identifier and status, not its biometric templates or decision documents. Configure the Didit workflow to require ID verification, liveness and face match.</p>
    <p>Seller application information is used only for identity checks and seller eligibility. Contact the admin team through <a class="link" href="<?= e(url('support.php')) ?>">Customer service</a> for privacy requests. This notice describes the app’s current handling and does not replace a review of applicable privacy-law obligations before launch.</p>

    <h2 class="h2" id="terms">Terms of use</h2>
    <p>By creating an account you agree to follow the <a class="link" href="<?= e(url('guidelines.php')) ?>">Community Guidelines</a>, to describe your items honestly, to meet buyers and sellers safely, and to let the admin team remove listings or restrict accounts that break the rules. Deals are arranged between buyers and sellers; the marketplace does not process payments.</p>
</section>
